# Global Quota Conservation Rule (Applies to ALL Models & ALL Projects)

## Core Principle
Minimize token consumption while maintaining code quality.

## File Operations
- View outline first: use `view_file_outline` before `view_file` for code files (when available).
- Targeted reads: specify `StartLine`/`EndLine` (or equivalent) to read only relevant sections.
- No re-reads: do not view files already seen in the conversation/session unless explicitly required.
- Code items: use `view_code_item` for specific functions/classes when available.

## Command Execution
- Auto-run safe commands: set `SafeToAutoRun=true` for read-only operations (e.g., `ls`, `grep`, `cat`), when the tool supports it.
- Batch operations: combine related commands into a single operation/script when possible.
- Limit output: use output limits/filters (e.g., `head -n 20`, `tail -n 50`, grep filters).
- Appropriate waits: set `WaitDurationSeconds` correctly; avoid aggressive polling.

## Search & Discovery
- Precise patterns: use specific globs with depth/pattern limits and appropriate excludes.
- Grep before view: search file contents before reading entire files.
- Case sensitivity: use `CaseInsensitive=false` for exact matches.

## Tool Call Optimization
- Parallel by default: run independent tool calls in parallel when supported.
- Sequential only when needed: enforce sequencing when dependencies exist.
- Batch file operations: move/copy multiple files in one command/script when possible.

## Workspace Hygiene
- Root directory target: keep fewer than 150 files in the project root (favor subfolders).
- Archive regularly: move test/debug/backup scripts into `archive/` (or an equivalent folder).
- Backup retention: keep only the last 7 days of database backups in the root.
- Compress archives: use `zip` for infrequently accessed files.

## Artifact Management
- Concise content: keep `task.md` / `implementation_plan.md` brief.
- Update, don't recreate: edit existing artifacts instead of creating new versions.
- Minimal metadata: avoid verbose summaries and repeated headers.

## Communication
- No filler: zero conversational pleasantries.
- Code-first: show code blocks directly when relevant.
- Bullet points: use lists instead of paragraphs when output is inherently list-shaped.
- Batch questions: ask all clarifications in one message.

## Anti-Patterns
- Do not read entire large files when only a section is needed.
- Do not view the same file multiple times.
- Do not run commands synchronously when parallel is safe.
- Do not search without depth/pattern limits.
- Do not keep 200+ test scripts in the workspace.
- Do not store all historical backups in the root.

